# Vercel builds from source; nothing here is input to that build.
#
# Written because `vercel deploy` aborted its upload against 2.4GB of local
# build output (.next 1.4G, .next-test 1.0G). These are gitignored, but the
# upload is the deploy's first step and making it explicit is cheaper than
# depending on that inference.
.next
.next-test
node_modules
test-results
playwright-report
coverage

# Test and review material: not needed to build or run the app. The unit
# tests that live beside their modules under src go too: `next build`
# type-checks the whole project, and eleven of them import fixtures and
# helpers from test/, which this file keeps out.
e2e
test
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.log

# Workbench routes: probes that render test fixtures at unlinked URLs and
# 404 in production by their own code. Left out of the upload so they are
# not built there either -- the first production build since the wall
# failed on their imports from test/, which this file keeps out.
# test/repo/src-imports-stay-in-src.test.ts holds the two together.
src/app/wall/probe

# Working documents: build history and review notes, not build input.
docs
NOTES.md
REVIEW-PLAN.md
